  "steps": [
    "Blend the whole jar of pickled jalapeños with their liquid until a thin, smooth, pale green puree.",
    "Whisk the mayonnaise, sour cream and all the sauce spices together, then stir in 7 tablespoons of the puree. Taste and add a little more puree if you like. Chill at least 1 hour.",
    "Slice each chicken breast horizontally into two thin fillets.",
    "Whisk the water, kosher salt, MSG, cornstarch and all the chicken spices and sugar until the cornstarch dissolves.",
    "Toss the chicken in the marinade, cover, and refrigerate for 30 to 45 minutes.",
    "Heat the oil in a skillet over medium-high heat and cook the chicken in batches, 3 to 4 minutes per side, until browned and 165°F inside.",
    "Rest the chicken 5 to 10 minutes, then chop it roughly into bite-size pieces.",
    "On one half of each tortilla layer cheese, chicken, a generous drizzle of creamy jalapeño sauce, then more cheese. Fold over.",
    "Cook in a griddle pan or skillet over medium heat (with a little butter if you like), pressing down with a weight, 90 seconds to 2 minutes per side until crisp and golden.",
    "Slice and serve with extra jalapeño sauce for dipping."
  ],
  "equipment": [
    "blender",
    "griddle pan"
  ],
  "tips": [
    "Add the jalapeño puree gradually; too much makes the sauce vinegary and very spicy.",
    "Press the quesadilla with a weight for even browning and a crisper tortilla.",
    "The sauce makes extra and keeps up to 14 days in the fridge; cooked chicken keeps 3 days."
  ],
